1)Create Management Group named MG1. In MG1 Create subscription and under subscription place Resource group named RG1
2)Create vnet named "On-Prem vnet" and subnet with 10.0.0.0/16 and 10.0.1.0/24 respectively and deploy VM with Standard_D8ds_v5 or Standard_E8ds_v5 with public IP address. Allow Default Port 3389 to VM for management
3)create vnet with name "vnet-hub-lab" with Address space 10.10.0.0/16 and subnet 10.10.1.0/24
3)Create VM extension to install Hyper-V role while provisioning VM
4) Inside Hyper-V host create 1 switches one for internal communication (Onprem-Internal ) and assign IP address to Hyper-V host NIC 192.168.100.1/24
5)Assign Nested VM static IP from 192.168.100.0/24 with default gateway 192.168.100.1. and Public DNS 4.4.4.4 or 8.8.8.8.

7)create vnet peering between "On-Prem vnet" and "vnet-hub-lab" with Allow IP forwarding enabled on both side.
8)Enable IP forwarding in Azure NIC and Hyper-V internal switch

$azIf = Get-NetAdapter | Where-Object { (Get-NetIPAddress -InterfaceIndex $_.ifIndex -AddressFamily IPv4 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).IPAddress -eq "10.0.1.4" }
Set-NetIPInterface -InterfaceIndex $vSwitchIf.ifIndex -Forwarding Enabled
Set-NetIPInterface -InterfaceIndex $azIf.ifIndex -Forwarding Enabled

9)Allow Routed Traffic through Windows Firewall on host

New-NetFirewallRule -DisplayName "Allow Nested 192.168.100.0/24 Routing" -Direction Inbound -AddressPrefix 192.168.100.0/24 -Action Allow
New-NetFirewallRule -DisplayName "Allow Outbound to Nested 192.168.100.0/24" -Direction Outbound -DestinationAddress 192.168.100.0/24 -Action Allow

